se is about","paragraphs":["The case asks whether a party can pause a main lawsuit by appealing an arbitration order. Coinbase wants the appeal to pause the main lawsuit. Bielski wants the main lawsuit to continue during the appeal."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 51, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 51, lines 23-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 13-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 13-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 88, lines 17-13","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 88, lines 17-13"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on March 21, 2023."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 11-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 11-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 71, lines 47-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 71, lines 47-7"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["Coinbase wants the appeal to pause the main lawsuit.","Bielski wants the main lawsuit to continue during the appeal."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 51, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 51, lines 23-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 13-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 13-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 88, lines 17-13","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 88, lines 17-13"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["Coinbase argues that the Federal Arbitration Act implies an automatic stay.","Bielski argues that the Federal Arbitration Act text does not mandate a stay."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 51, lines 23-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 51, lines 23-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 13-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2022/22-105_i32c.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 13-23"},{"evidence_type":"